Lethe patch absolutely great; makes the game from the castle on down
way more interesting and challenging.

But - how do you cope with the ranged summon attack, without
genociding spellcasters? (individually, because blessed genocide
always seems to leave them behind, especially L's :)

First time I was in the castle basement (as a W), detect monster shows
a vampire mage just the other side of some doors; head towards him,
suddenly there's 8 assorted dragons, hulks, etc. around me. Couple of
turns later I'm about 6 deep in monsters, including a bunch of liches
and magii of various stripes all spellcasting as well; I escape but
run into similar problems elsewhere.

In the end, I give up trying to be genoless and take out as many of
the spellcasting monsters as I can remember; the other solution is
conflict, but I try to avoid using that as well. But other than that,
is there any good way to deal with ranged (through walls :) summoning?
Having to kill an entire screen of monsters several times every level
of Gehennom gets a bit wearing...

